{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119073-the-grand-unification-theory-just-for-fun","id":1119073,"title":"The Grand Unification Theory [Just For Fun]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-21T14:17:49-07:00","id":1119073,"title":"The Grand Unification Theory [Just For Fun]","content":"I've thought about something.<br /> <br /> I'm not a &quot;Mage Supremacist&quot;. I don't think that everything should be explained through Mage's cosmology, or that cosmology is 100% true (more of 50% of it), or that mages simply know everything about the whole world as they are the best investigators in the whole setting. However, it can not be denied that they are good investigators, and as such they have noticed certain.. trends, like how it seems like each major supernatural &quot;specie&quot; could be divided into a number of &quot;sub types&quot;, with the number of said sub-types being around 4-7. Call it Clans, Seemings or Auspices, but each of those sub-types has some specific features which makes it different from the other types. Now, mages know why they are divided in that way- each is Awakened to a different Watchtower, and each draws upon a different Supernal Realm. What if the reason that the other Supernals divide themselves the way they do is also tied to the five Supernal Realms? What is they, too, walk their own &quot;Path&quot; toward Ascension?<br /> <br /> That's madness! How self absorbed one has to be in order to make such ridiculous claims?<br /> <br /> Well, mages could be self absorbed sometimes, you know?<br /> <br /> That's not meant to be &quot;true&quot; in any kind of form- but we can assume that at least one Cabal has thought about that theory. Or maybe even a Nameless Order. Maybe there is an whole Legacy based around that theory, which is dedicated into mapping the impossible and interacting with the other supernatural denizens of the world. And even if their theory is all upside down, maybe some of the things they do actually works- not all of it, just enough to support their claims. Maybe they are just crazy nomads who travel the world in search for evidence for their theory. Maybe their are an aggressive group, which use those claims as an excuse to force their rule upon other supernatural creatures. Perhaps they are both. At any case, If I were to map each of the X-splat of the different templates into the Supernal Realms, here is how I would have done it-<br /> <br /> Arcadia- Path Acanthus, Clan Daeva, House Irinavici Cahalith Auspice, Galateid Lineage, Fairest Seeming, Forgotten Threshold, Name Decree, Poet Temakh, Messenger Incarnation, Family Ugallu, Aegis Kai Doru<br /> <br /> Aether- Path Obrimos, Clan Ventrue, House Semeonovic, Elodoth Auspice, Frankenstein Lineage, Elemental Seeming, Silent Threshold, Essence Decree, Musician Temakh, Destroyer Incarnation, Family Anakim, Malleus Maleficarum<br /> <br /> Primal Wild- Path Thyrsus, Clan Gangrel, House Grigorovich, Irraka Auspice, Ulgan Lineage, Beast Seeming, Prey Threshold, Spirit Decree, Keeper Temakh, Psychopomp Incarnation, Family Eshmaki, Les Mysteres<br /> <br /> Stygia- Path Moros, Clan Mekhet, House Marisovich, Ithaeur Auspice, Osirian Lineage, Darkling Seeming, Stricken Threshold, Shadow Decree, Philosopher Temakh, Analyst Incarnation, Family Makara, Ascending Ones<br /> <br /> Pandemonium- Path Mastigos, Clan Nosferatu, House Alexander, Rahu Auspice, Tammuz Lineage, Ogre Seeming, Torn Threshold, Heart Decree, Singer Temakh, Guardian Incarnation, Family Namtaru, Lucifuge<br /> <br /> Of course, there are some holes in that theory- with the main one being that, actually, the number of existing sub-type does not match the number of Paths. Many of the supernatural has extinct splats (like Lost Clans) or minor strains (like the Grim Seeming)- and even if we remove them from the equation, we still have exceptions to the rule (6 Seemings, 4 main Incarnations, god knows how many Conspiracies). For most people with good critical thinking, it should be enough to throw that theory to the garbage. On the other hand, mages are famous for having a good critical thinking- more than one has shown a measure of mental instability, and spending your entire life accepting that reality is a Lie and only you know the Truth surely doesn't help. Some mages, instead of recognizing the flaws of their theory, would probably try to force that theory upon reality. After all, some of those splats have died and were &quot;replaced&quot;- like certain lost Clans and Lineages. That may mean that because only one kind of supernatural being may exist per realm, the rise of a new splat caused the death of the former (or perhaps the death of the former caused the rise of the later? who knows if time is truly linear, after all). Others may say that the extra splats are actually signs of new, unknown Supernal Realms and Paths. Everyone heard the rumors about a sixth Watchtower made of Brass which rules over a realm of Djinn. What if the extra splats are tuned to it, or some other hidden realm? Some even dare to say that those types are not true members of their &quot;family&quot;. They are mockeries, created by the Lie, twisted creations of the Exarch, the Lower Depths or some Abyssal intruder, and as such should be exterminated so only the &quot;five pure breeds&quot; could exist. Some, however, whisper that there is another option- that some of those sub types are attuned to the Abyss itself, just as the others are tuned to the Supernal, as if the Abyss was a Supernal Realm by itself.<br /> <br /> And in that case, shouldn't be a Path for those who walk the Abyss?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T15:44:54-07:00","id":1119094,"title":"","content":"What are &quot;Houses&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T16:03:07-07:00","id":1119098,"title":"","content":"Why have the Deceived on there when their origins are well-known and they number Seven, not Five?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"ke