y it's just for fun, and since the CoD cosmology is deliberately twisted to be irreconcilable there isn't really any point in ripping a doomed attempt at understanding apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T00:43:18-07:00","id":1119201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119073-the-grand-unification-theory-just-for-fun?p=1119094#post1119094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are &quot;Houses&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>an optional VII Clan like system<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Why have the Deceived on there when their origins are well-known and they number Seven, not Five?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>because that theory is flawed and makes no sense from its very core? I've wrote about it in the opening post<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts from Changeling are more likely to bust through the thorns of the Acanthus Path than the Fairest. Fairest are more akin to the Mastigos or Obrimos</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some of the Decrees doesn't correspond to the Path's associated Subtle Arcanum. Also I would have put the Auspices in a totally different way. Elodoth with all their deal making powers seem more akin to Achantus, Cahalith if anything closer to Pandemonium, etc. But I suppose everyone would have their preferences. <br /> <br /> Not a bad mental exercise though.</div> </div> </div> </div>like I've said, it is merely an optional list. We can safely assume that if there is such theory in the setting, each Cabal would have it own preferences about where to put each X splat. I can totally see mages who debate about whether the Fairest are about Aether or Arcadia, and if one should map the Torn to the Primal Wild or Pandemonium. Feel free to suggest your own!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did say it's just for fun, and since the CoD cosmology is deliberately twisted to be irreconcilable there isn't really any point in ripping a doomed attempt at understanding apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.stor